theory.intro:
A **diagonal** joins two vertices of a quadrilateral that are not next to each other. Use the known properties of the shape and the given marks to describe its diagonals. **Bisect** means cut into two equal parts.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0.4);
\coordinate (B) at (1.2,3);
\coordinate (C) at (4.4,2.4);
\coordinate (D) at (3.6,0);
\draw (A) -- (B) -- (C) -- (D) -- cycle;
\draw[dashed] (A) -- (C);
\draw[dashed] (B) -- (D);
\node[left] at (A) {$A$};
\node[above left] at (B) {$B$};
\node[above right] at (C) {$C$};
\node[below right] at (D) {$D$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

